appeal_text:
Hello friends, family and neighbors,
On Oct 23rd, Alex, Doug, Liam and Zach lost everything in a house fire.
The fire happened around 1pm and some of the roommates were home, heard the smoke detectors and called the fire department.
We are very fortunate that there are no injuries but everyone lost pretty much everything they owned. Due to a misunderstanding, some of them didn't have renters insurance so this fund is to help them get back on their feet.
For the time being everyone has a place to sleep and basic needs are met. Alex is staying with his girlfriend in San Francisco and working as a software solution architect. Doug is staying at his dads house in Santa Cruz and is working as a sales engineer. Liam just moved back to San Francisco about a month ago after a few years of traveling and working abroad, is still looking for a job and is currently staying with his parents in Davis. Zach is working for a non-profit in the bay and staying with his parents in Fresno.
You can reach out to them on Instagram
@a.b.ly
@Dougggie_fresssh
@liamhedriana
@zantoyan
Please make sure you have fire extinguishers and know how to use them. Please put fresh batteries into your smoke detectors. Please make sure your renters or homeowners insurance is up to date, paid for and covers your belongings! Please also take photos and videos of everything in your home. It's very difficult to photograph when it's reduced to ash.
Thanks so much for your donation, it means the world to them and anything helps during this challenging time!

Hi! My name is Reye (or Mother Macabre) and I’m making this fundraiser in desperation to save my friend and channel artist Kazumi (please do not tell her she’s going to be pissed)
I am terrified for her. I am terrified for her mental health, and for her physical well-being. She’s from Brazil and if you know anything about Brazil well…yeah. But she’s also a victim of abuse and cannot get away, she can barely make enough to cover bills, and she is reaching dangerous levels of exhaustion that I am shaking as I write this from the things she tells me in private. I need to do something that will let her be able to afford her way out of there, or to at least give her relief from working herself to death for a few months, and give her the chance to actually rest and heal. Please anything will help, I’m just so afraid, I love her so much. I know times are tough but I don’t know what else to do. I’m afraid I’ll lose her. This is the only thing I can think of to help. But if you’re coming here from my channel, then just know she is the other half of my channel, she’s just as important to it as I am, and she needs all of us right now, please, o don’t know what else to do <3 thank you for your time and understanding 
and Kazumi if you do end up finding this and are reading this, IM SORRY! YOU MAKE ME SCARED AND I JUST NEED TO HELP YOU, PLEASE FORGIVE ME I know you wouldn’t have ever asked for this, BUT IM CRYING FOR YOU ;0;

This is a two-part campaign supporting the Southbound McKnight Road Starbucks partners of Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania (store location 7707 McKnight Rd). We the workers insist that our demands be met:     attain and properly train staff so that we may easily meet our store’s level of business;      the ability to take breaks throughout our shifts as they are scheduled on the schedule itself;      ensure that when scheduled outside of our accepted work availability, upper management understands it is solely their job to fill scheduling gaps and that our jobs should not be held as leverage for their own mistakes;
     provide required extensive one-on-one training for partners who are promoted within the company instead of scheduling them and expecting that they figure the job out as they work;
     assist our fellow partner, Julia, with job relocation*;       and
     lastly, Starbucks is required to recognize our union, meet with us, and bargain with us in good faith rather than promising to meet with us on a given date and canceling last minute. In order to protest the treatment we’ve received from corporate, we have decided to perform a ULP strike. While our union provides those of us who show up to strike 70% of our wages for the day, we would like to reach 100% for each partner. There are fourteen of us scheduled this day, and to meet 100% of our wages, we each would need approximately $20 a piece. This brings us to the total of $280 to cover the wage disparity for our strike. *The second part of our campaign is dedicated to Julia Boatright. She has been a Starbucks partner for multiple years, and she has three young children who she cares for with the help of her significant other. Recently, her family was completely displaced due to a house fire. In light of this event, a partner at our store elected to start a partner-only donation jar to be placed in the back of house in order raise funds for Julia. Our management team stated that this was unacceptable, against Starbucks policy, and considered solicitation. Julia’s only option was to move an hour away from our workplace to stay with relatives. In attempting to figure out how to move forward, Julia spoke with our store manager about the possibility of transferring stores. He told her that, because the transferring process would be “difficult”, it would be best if she quit and then reapplied. Doing this would mean she forfeits insurance benefits, built up stock, and seniority, which factors into her pay rate. Further, he stated that if she does not take a leave of absence (which, per Starbucks policy, can only be done once every three years), he would proceed by terminating her. Our campaign fund is $500 because, past the $280 for our striking wages, we want to support Julia. Every dollar over the $280 mark would go to her, her family, and a potential new home. Julia deserves to be treated with grace, kindness, and dignity, and if corporate and our management team will not afford her those simple things, her work family will. 
Thank you for reading what we have to say and for considering supporting our cause. We love you, Julia. In solidarity.
